    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## AI Chat Evaluation  \r\n\r\nThis chatbot is an AI feedback assistant trained to help you evaluate and improve your **Network Security Risk Assessment**. It provides structured feedback on the clarity, realism, ethical reasoning, and AI fit of your project so you can strengthen your final draft.  \r\n\r\n### Do This:\r\n\r\n1. Upload your **AI Security Tool Design** or summarize your main ideas.  \r\n2. Ask the chatbot:  \r\n   - Explain how clearly the **vulnerability** is described. Do any specific details make it understandable or confusing?  \r\n   - Explain whether my **proposed solution** is realistic and detailed enough. How could it be stronger?  \r\n   - Explain how well the **societal or ethical impacts** have been described. What could make these descriptions stronger?  \r\n   - Explain how the **AI tool** I’ve designed fits the vulnerability I’ve identified. How clear and responsible is AI’s role in my solution?  \r\n3. Record the AI’s feedback and your **reflections or revisions** in your **AI Chat Evaluation Organizer.**\r\n\r\n::: details [**Need help refining your questions?**]\r\nUse these prompts to help the AI give clearer, more specific feedback:\r\n- Which parts of my explanation are most confusing or unclear?  \r\n- How realistic is my proposed solution for this scenario?  \r\n- What ethical or social concerns might I be overlooking?  \r\n- How could I make the AI’s role in my solution more transparent or responsible?  \r\n- What are the biggest strengths and weaknesses in my design overall?  \r\n:::\r\n",
    "aichat_settings": {
      "initialCustomizations": {
        "selectedModelId": "gpt-4o-mini",
        "temperature": 0.3,
        "systemPrompt": "",
        "retrievalContexts": [

        ],
        "modelCardInfo": {
          "botName": "AI Chat Evaluation Assistant",
          "description": "The AI Chat Evaluation Assistant is a specialized chatbot designed to help students evaluate and refine their Network Security Risk Assessments, including the AI-powered security tools they’ve designed.\nIt provides structured, constructive feedback focused on four key dimensions of effective cybersecurity analysis:\n- Clarity of Vulnerability – Evaluates how well the network risk is explained.\n\n- Realism of Solution – Assesses whether proposed traditional and AI-driven solutions are feasible and well-detailed.\n\n- Societal & Ethical Impact – Analyzes the depth and accuracy of the ethical reasoning in\ncluded.\n\nAI Tool Fit & Responsibility – Examines how appropriately the AI tool aligns with the identified vulnerability and whether its role is responsible and transparent.\n\nThis chatbot supports critical evaluation, reflection, and revision, helping students manage AI feedback responsibly and strengthen both the technical and ethical quality of their final projects. ",
          "intendedUse": "- Educational feedback assistant for students completing AI-enhanced cybersecurity projects\n- Tool for teaching Managing AI competencies, including responsible evaluation and refinement of AI outputs\n- Structured guide for assessing the quality, realism, and ethics of student-designed AI systems\n- Classroom support for revising Network Security Risk Assessments based on AI-generated feedback\n- Resource for reinforcing critical thinking about AI’s strengths, limits, and appropriate use",
          "limitationsAndWarnings": "- Not a grading or scoring system – The chatbot provides qualitative feedback, not numerical evaluation or grades.\n- No live security assessment – It cannot detect or analyze real cybersecurity threats.\n- No real-time verification – The AI does not fact-check data or confirm technical accuracy beyond conceptual reasoning.\n- Educational purpose only – Designed for reflection and revision within the classroom context.\\\n- Human judgment required – Students must interpret, question, and decide how to apply AI feedback rather than accepting it at face value.",
          "testingAndEvaluation": "- Accuracy Testing: Confirm that AI feedback aligns with the student’s content and addresses all four focus areas accurately.\n- Balance Testing: Ensure responses provide both positive reinforcement and constructive critique.\n- Bias Testing: Verify that the AI evaluates ideas fairly, without promoting AI as infallible or dismissing human oversight.\n- Clarity Testing: Check that feedback is phrased in student-friendly, specific, and actionable language.\n- Educational Effectiveness: Collect classroom feedback to ensure the AI’s guidance helps students produce clearer, more responsible final assessments.",
          "exampleTopics": [
            "Explain how clearly my vulnerability is described. What could make it clearer?",
            "Is my proposed solution realistic and detailed enough? How could it be stronger?",
            "How well do I describe the societal or ethical impacts of this vulnerability?",
            "Does my AI tool fit the vulnerability I identified? How responsible is AI’s role in my solution?",
            "What are the biggest strengths and weaknesses in my final risk assessment?"
          ],
          "isPublished": false
        }
      },
      "visibilities": {
